  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">All 4 Life &#x2013; Inclusive Sustainable Livelihoods for Small-Scale Farmers in Northern Uganda</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">All 4 Life &#x2013; Inclusive Sustainable Livelihoods for Small-Scale Farmers in Northern Uganda.
This intervention empowers 1,550 rural farmer families, 60 church leaders, and 3,000 church members from 20 churches in Lira, Kole, and Masindi through a holistic, faith-based approach. Drawing on Christian stewardship values, the project integrates sustainable agriculture (Farming God&#x2019;s Way), health education, and Village Savings and Loan Associations (VSLAs). Local churches lead environmental action through the Green Church initiative, promoting climate adaptation and advocacy. A cooperative will strengthen farmers&#x2019; economic rights and access to markets. Rooted in diaconal values and community participation, the project fosters dignity, self-reliance, and long-term impact.</narrative>
  </description>
